WEBVTT

00:01.920 --> 00:05.760
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.270
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.580 --> 00:15.430
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.430 --> 00:20.720
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.720 --> 00:25.270
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.900
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.900 --> 00:34.090
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.630
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.330 --> 02:16.990
<b>Remnant of the Divinity: The Aberrant Loser</b>

02:22.550 --> 02:26.050
Anyway, the game was the 
buggiest piece of crap,

02:26.050 --> 02:28.810
and the only save was autosave!

02:28.810 --> 02:31.080
I don't really follow, 
but it sounds pretty fun!

02:31.080 --> 02:32.740
Nope, not fun at all.

02:32.740 --> 02:34.460
Game crash bugs.

02:35.030 --> 02:36.300
The worst kind of trash!

02:36.610 --> 02:38.650
Then why are you playing it?

02:38.650 --> 02:39.650
It's fun!

02:39.650 --> 02:40.470
Hey.

02:40.950 --> 02:43.110
<i>He was always smiling.</i>

02:53.560 --> 02:56.250
Hey, Rakuro. Is that the latest issue?

02:56.970 --> 02:58.170
What now?

02:58.170 --> 03:00.230
More trash game scouting?

02:58.170 --> 03:00.230
<i>He seemed to be enjoying himself.</i>

03:14.530 --> 03:18.610
<i>That's why I started thinking about him.</i>

03:27.390 --> 03:30.890
<i>I started looking for him.</i>

03:50.120 --> 03:51.690
'Sup, Rakuro?

03:51.690 --> 03:52.270
Heya.

03:52.270 --> 03:54.880
<i>I tried to talk to him so many times...</i>

03:52.300 --> 03:54.170
Up all night gaming again?

03:54.170 --> 03:55.820
As a matter of fact...

03:55.820 --> 03:57.850
<i>But I wasn't brave enough.</i>

03:55.820 --> 03:59.200
Listen to this, man! 
Talk about a nightmare...

03:58.170 --> 04:01.060
<i>I thought, if I could just 
talk to Hizutome-kun...</i>

03:59.200 --> 04:01.550
Trashiest trash game ever...

04:02.010 --> 04:05.270
<i>Even if it was inside a game...</i>

04:08.320 --> 04:09.420
Damn it!

04:09.420 --> 04:12.420
This god-tier game doesn't 
need a trash game arc!

04:17.130 --> 04:20.660
I'm gonna make you cough up that info!

04:24.390 --> 04:27.900
Severing attack! Rook-smasher!

04:31.850 --> 04:34.000
Wh-What in the world?!

04:36.670 --> 04:39.300
<i>Psyger-0</i>

04:37.190 --> 04:39.300
<i>Psyger-0.</i>

04:39.760 --> 04:41.980
<i>Doesn't look like the PKing type...</i>

04:42.660 --> 04:45.330
<i>But I'll bet they're after the unique 
scenario, same as the others.</i>

04:45.800 --> 04:48.300
<i>I'm never getting out of this.</i>

04:48.570 --> 04:50.890
<i>I need to think up a way out.</i>

04:54.810 --> 04:58.340
Can you counter my final hand?!

04:59.920 --> 05:04.880
It requires the skill 
"Spell Mastery" and single-digit HP.

05:03.570 --> 05:08.070
<b>Poison      Paralysis          Drain          Exhaustion         Speed</b>

05:04.880 --> 05:08.070
A murder-suicide curse to destroy 
both my opponent and myself!

05:08.830 --> 05:11.450
<i>I've used up the Karmic Straw Doll.</i>

05:11.450 --> 05:13.620
<i>I can't reflect another curse!</i>

05:14.250 --> 05:16.540
I'll trade out my remaining life,

05:16.540 --> 05:18.780
I'll inflict the "Insta-Death" debuff!

05:18.520 --> 05:21.920
<b>See you in Hell,
Fellow Traveler!</b>

05:18.780 --> 05:20.890
Fellow Traveler!

05:23.030 --> 05:24.490
Well, drat.

05:27.450 --> 05:28.330
What the...

05:28.330 --> 05:29.350
Pencilgon-san?!

05:34.850 --> 05:36.640
Emul. Get a gate ready.

05:36.640 --> 05:37.850
Gwuh?!

05:44.650 --> 05:45.780
Sorry.

05:54.790 --> 05:55.600
Hey!

05:55.600 --> 05:57.250
D-Damn it!

05:57.250 --> 06:00.130
You left yourself wide open, dumbass!

06:05.590 --> 06:07.450
Don't let him reach the city!

06:07.450 --> 06:09.390
It's swarming with bounty hunters!

06:14.970 --> 06:17.480
<i>Psyger-0</i>

06:15.460 --> 06:17.480
<i>I'll remember your name, at least...</i>

06:18.340 --> 06:19.640
<i>Psyger-0.</i>

06:26.500 --> 06:29.170
Damn it! Attack Master!

06:29.170 --> 06:31.280
You think you can just get in our way?!

06:31.280 --> 06:33.730
Don't look down on the Ashura Kai!

06:37.460 --> 06:39.160
Sorry.

06:39.160 --> 06:40.540
Sorry.

06:40.540 --> 06:42.090
Sorry.

06:42.720 --> 06:43.740
Sorry.

06:47.150 --> 06:50.620
<i>He talked to me!</i>

06:51.240 --> 06:53.690
That guy's acting pretty weird, right?

06:53.690 --> 06:55.180
What's going on?

06:55.590 --> 06:58.640
I dunno, but he's wide open.

06:58.640 --> 06:59.440
Now's our chance!

06:59.900 --> 07:04.440
PKing you will have me shooting 
up the Ashura Kai ranks!

07:04.780 --> 07:08.000
<i>But if not for you people...</i>

07:08.000 --> 07:10.440
<i>I could have talked to him more!</i>

07:13.540 --> 07:14.850
Make a break for it?

07:14.850 --> 07:15.910
Yep.

07:16.650 --> 07:18.750
Sorry, but I'll have to—

07:19.090 --> 07:22.890
I mean, I'm taking my rage out on you!

07:30.050 --> 07:31.190
Rabituza Inn

07:32.170 --> 07:34.050
Yes! I escaped!

07:35.210 --> 07:36.460
Well?

07:36.460 --> 07:38.310
How'd you like that, 
you basement-dwelling bastards?!

07:38.750 --> 07:41.160
They can't follow me to Rabituza!

07:44.760 --> 07:47.030
That was pretty scary, though!

07:47.030 --> 07:47.920
Didn't expect that

07:47.920 --> 07:50.980
"Gracious! I have insufficient magic 
for a gate!" from you, though.

07:53.000 --> 07:55.530
I used it all on my transformation!

07:55.530 --> 07:58.950
We'd have been in real trouble if 
we couldn't travel from Thirdrema.

07:59.210 --> 08:01.310
This is truly delicious!

08:01.310 --> 08:04.930
Good thing I bought some 
magic-restoring items.

08:04.930 --> 08:08.190
Anyway, objective accomplished.

08:09.460 --> 08:15.970
Okay, You Got Me
 From: Pencil Knight
 To: Sunraku
 Nice job escaping those scrubs. 
 FYI, my death was my own fault,
so I don't consider this losing to you. 
 Can't believe the Attack Master came
to bail you out. Friend of yours?
 Anyway, I really do want to talk to you,
so call Katzo-kun for a meeting in <i>Unite Rounds</i>.
We'll talk scheduling later.

08:10.020 --> 08:15.970
Pencil Knight... I mean, Pencilgon 
sent me a sore loser email.

08:16.380 --> 08:21.380
<i>FYI, my death was my own fault, 
so I don't consider this losing to you.</i>

08:21.380 --> 08:25.070
<i>Can't believe the 
Attack Master came to bail you out.</i>

08:25.070 --> 08:26.300
<i>Friend of yours?</i>

08:26.830 --> 08:28.580
"Attack Master"?

08:29.030 --> 08:31.490
That Psyger-0 person?

08:32.130 --> 08:36.080
<i>Anyway, I really do want to talk to you,</i>

08:36.080 --> 08:39.130
<i>so call Katzo-kun for a 
meeting in </i>Unite Rounds<i>.</i>

08:39.470 --> 08:40.950
<i>We'll talk scheduling later.</i>

08:41.500 --> 08:43.360
Talk to me, eh?

08:43.810 --> 08:46.960
The fact that she won't talk inside <i>SLF</i>...

08:47.290 --> 08:48.770
Makes me suspicious.

08:49.370 --> 08:51.960
Hey, speak of the devil.

08:51.960 --> 09:00.850
Hey
 From: Modor Katzo
 To: Sunraku
 Just got a total "evil mastermind"
invite from the pencil. What'd you do, man?
 Can't say I'm not intrigued, so I figure
we might as well hear her out.
You're not gonna back out, right?

08:52.570 --> 08:59.040
<i>Just got a total "evil mastermind" 
invite from the pencil.</i>

08:59.040 --> 09:00.850
<i>What'd you do, man?</i>

09:01.220 --> 09:03.370
<i>It's fishy as hell...</i>

09:03.920 --> 09:06.850
<i>but it's equally intriguing, if I'm honest.</i>

09:06.850 --> 09:11.210
<i>Can't say I'm not intrigued, so I 
figure we might as well hear her out.</i>

09:11.210 --> 09:13.450
<i>You're not gonna back out, right?</i>

09:13.980 --> 09:17.660
Well, I can't back out after 
Katzo starts adding pressure, too.

09:18.010 --> 09:20.580
But I've got bigger things 
to think about now.

09:22.160 --> 09:23.930
What a lovely treat!

09:23.930 --> 09:25.620
Sorry for the wait, Emul.

09:26.560 --> 09:29.660
Let's get to this unique scenario for real!

09:29.660 --> 09:31.350
Oh, at last!

09:31.350 --> 09:33.860
Hurrah, hurrah!

09:36.000 --> 09:38.110
So, what's the task?

09:38.940 --> 09:40.650
That Vash guy...

09:40.650 --> 09:44.980
I mean, your bunny boss, said something 
about "getting me up to snuff."

09:46.410 --> 09:52.730
Then I shall lead you to the arena where 
we do our most serious battle training!

09:52.950 --> 09:54.610
Arena?

09:54.670 --> 09:58.610
Vorpal Colosseum

10:03.900 --> 10:06.370
The Vorpal Colosseum!

10:06.370 --> 10:09.630
Hey, that's pretty big!

10:09.630 --> 10:16.700
My dadd—ahem, the boss wants 
you to fight ten monsters here!

10:16.700 --> 10:17.810
Okay!

10:17.810 --> 10:20.640
So it's a boss rush kind of thing, right?

10:21.030 --> 10:25.310
Ah, but you are strictly limited 
to the use of vorpal weapons!

10:25.310 --> 10:26.580
Great!

10:26.580 --> 10:27.890
Okay!

10:28.610 --> 10:36.070
Time to grind levels until I can wipe 
that smug smirk off of Pencilgon's face!

10:39.490 --> 10:40.950
All ready.

10:44.700 --> 10:46.720
Let out the first one!

10:46.720 --> 10:47.750
Righty-o!

10:47.750 --> 10:50.820
Here it comes!

10:52.400 --> 10:56.600
<i>I don't expect to go ten 
in a row on my first try.</i>

10:56.600 --> 11:02.090
<i>I'll use trial and error, learn their 
attack patterns, and slowly but surely...</i>

11:05.660 --> 11:15.020
Practical Training  Opponent 1
Packhound
Always spawns in groups of 5 or more

Average Level <b>65</b>

11:06.490 --> 11:08.760
<i>Practical training, opponent 1.</i>

11:08.760 --> 11:10.440
<i>Packhound.</i>

11:10.440 --> 11:12.830
<i>Always spawns in groups of five or more.</i>

11:12.830 --> 11:15.020
<i>Average level, 65.</i>

11:15.980 --> 11:17.780
<i>Looks tough.</i>

11:18.170 --> 11:19.410
Hang on a minute here!

11:19.410 --> 11:22.030
You're making me fight 
multiple enemies over level 65?!

11:22.810 --> 11:25.300
Well, of course!

11:25.300 --> 11:26.870
That's how the first opponent works!

11:28.370 --> 11:32.000
A-At least say first <i>fight</i>, not <i>opponent!</i>

11:39.010 --> 11:42.510
<b>Constant Progress</b>

11:44.430 --> 11:47.120
I talked to Hizutome-kun!

11:53.760 --> 11:54.810
Sorry.

12:00.740 --> 12:02.910
N-Next time I see him,

12:02.910 --> 12:06.520
I'll try to find the courage 
to send a friend request.

12:07.510 --> 12:10.350
I wonder if he'd accept it...

12:12.410 --> 12:13.980
A friend request?

12:16.750 --> 12:18.990
Of course I'll accept!

12:20.100 --> 12:24.740
Psyger-0, I can't thank you 
enough for saving me back there.

12:25.290 --> 12:27.760
Let's walk to school together every morning!

12:29.720 --> 12:31.140
Oh, you silly!

12:40.730 --> 12:45.770
But I entered Thirdrema and looked 
for him after it was over,

12:46.160 --> 12:48.170
and I couldn't find him...

12:48.890 --> 12:51.240
Did he log out, maybe?

12:53.810 --> 12:57.090
I wonder what he's doing now.

12:58.870 --> 13:02.260
These guys... totally...

13:02.260 --> 13:04.260
just think of me as food!

13:04.260 --> 13:07.810
Sunraku-san! It's your seventh try!

13:07.810 --> 13:10.530
This time, see that you beat them!

13:10.970 --> 13:15.200
<i>Thankfully, the penalty for 
dying is off here in the arena.</i>

13:15.200 --> 13:19.390
<i>But it's not their numbers and 
level that make these guys a pain.</i>

13:19.390 --> 13:21.950
<i>It's their completely 
synchronized team attacks!</i>

13:21.950 --> 13:23.400
Repel Counter!

13:23.840 --> 13:27.780
<i>That coordination is the result of 
having a commander giving orders!</i>

13:27.780 --> 13:29.020
Slide Move!

13:32.430 --> 13:36.210
<i>I've fought them enough times 
that I've started to see it...</i>

13:36.620 --> 13:39.090
<i>One monster that keeps howling 
from a safe distance,</i>

13:39.090 --> 13:41.710
<i>and never actually attacks!</i>

13:43.380 --> 13:45.340
You're the commander, aren't you?!

13:47.060 --> 13:49.010
Spiral Edge!

13:49.010 --> 13:51.410
<b>Spiral Edge</b>

13:58.020 --> 13:59.760
Looks like I guessed right!

13:59.760 --> 14:01.770
Your coordination's all out of whack!

14:02.020 --> 14:05.610
And now that I know that, 
I can ignore these suckers!

14:05.610 --> 14:09.320
I'll focus on the commander 
before he can bark out orders!

14:09.320 --> 14:10.510
Get back here, you!

14:13.130 --> 14:14.160
Gotcha!

14:19.370 --> 14:21.920
Impressive as ever, Sunraku-san!

14:22.400 --> 14:26.240
Monsters left on their own 
after losing their commander

14:26.240 --> 14:27.970
are nothing for me to fear!

14:33.290 --> 14:36.390
Once you know the trick, 
they're just durable dogs.

14:36.390 --> 14:39.090
You're brilliant, Sunraku-san!

14:39.090 --> 14:43.980
<i>Practical training, opponent 1: 
Packhound, complete.</i>

14:39.500 --> 14:45.230
Practical Training  Opponent 1
Packhound
Always spawns in groups of 5 or more

Average Level <b>65</b>

14:43.980 --> 14:45.230
<b>Complete</b>

14:45.610 --> 14:48.420
Excellent work, Sunraku-san!

14:48.420 --> 14:50.950
The next one's not a group, too, is it?

14:50.950 --> 14:53.950
The next one is definitely a single opponent!

14:54.250 --> 14:56.290
It'd better be, man.

15:02.310 --> 15:06.840
Practical Training  Opponent 2
Parasite Tentacle

15:02.490 --> 15:06.480
<i>Practical training, opponent 2: 
Parasite Tentacle.</i>

15:08.840 --> 15:11.520
It's basically another freaking group!

15:14.310 --> 15:18.530
<i>Like the name implied, the real monster 
was the tentacles, not the bear.</i>

15:18.530 --> 15:21.940
<i>I kept up a hit-and-run 
strategy on the tentacles,</i>

15:21.940 --> 15:25.980
<i>and once the seventh was severed, 
the bear stopped moving and I won.</i>

15:25.880 --> 15:27.460
<b>Defeated on
4th try</b>

15:26.840 --> 15:38.450
Practical Training  Opponent 3
Goblin Berserker

15:27.820 --> 15:31.880
<i>"A really tough goblin" 
is the only way to put it.</i>

15:32.190 --> 15:34.530
<i>Tough or not, though, 
he's still just a goblin.</i>

15:34.530 --> 15:37.310
<i>He was easier than the 
wolves or the tentacles.</i>

15:36.760 --> 15:38.790
<b>Defeated on
2nd try</b>

15:38.390 --> 16:01.620
Practical Training  Opponent 4
Dinoboar

15:38.840 --> 15:40.490
<i>This boar sucks.</i>

15:40.490 --> 15:45.280
<i>Its ability to blow you up if its nose 
hits you while it's charging wasn't that bad.</i>

15:45.280 --> 15:47.780
<i>But it's got crazy stamina.</i>

15:48.230 --> 15:53.050
<i>I timed it, and it ran about 
twenty seconds on each charge.</i>

15:53.050 --> 15:57.230
<i>If not for my rodeo experience, 
it would've taken way longer.</i>

15:58.280 --> 16:00.490
<i>That's in-game rodeo experience, by the way.</i>

16:00.370 --> 16:02.040
<b>Defeated on
1st try</b>

16:01.810 --> 16:10.070
Practical Training  Opponent 5
Toxic Eagle

16:02.610 --> 16:05.780
You'll pay. Oh, you <i>will</i> pay.

16:06.380 --> 16:08.840
Sunraku-san!

16:08.840 --> 16:10.510
<b>Defeated on
112th try</b>

16:09.840 --> 16:22.210
Practical Training  Opponent 6
Armored Larva

16:10.620 --> 16:14.000
You're a simpleton compared 
to the birdy bastard

16:14.000 --> 16:18.080
who hovered out of attack range 
while dropping poison bombs.

16:18.080 --> 16:20.990
Spend your whole life on the 
ground, never growing wings.

16:20.470 --> 16:22.520
<b>Defeated on
1st try</b>

16:21.890 --> 16:34.320
Practical Training  Opponent 7
Execu-panther

16:22.690 --> 16:25.220
<i>Fast and strong but not too tough.</i>

16:25.610 --> 16:29.610
<i>Once you learn that its strategy 
is to get around behind you and</i>

16:29.610 --> 16:33.140
<i>attack from outside your sight line, 
it's easy to take down.</i>

16:32.650 --> 16:34.610
<b>Defeated on
1st try</b>

16:34.340 --> 16:41.490
Practical Training  Opponent 8
Twinhead Tiger

16:34.960 --> 16:38.920
<i>Not great, not terrible. 
Just a pretty strong guy.</i>

16:39.450 --> 16:40.420
<i>That's it.</i>

16:40.240 --> 16:41.790
<b>Defeated on
2nd try</b>

16:41.580 --> 16:43.080
Practical Training  Opponent 9
Beta Unit Golem S2

16:42.480 --> 16:48.160
<i>If we call attacks from the right arm A, 
and attacks from the left arm B,</i>

16:48.160 --> 16:52.410
<i>when chaining from A to A, 
there's almost no gap between its attacks.</i>

16:52.410 --> 16:55.880
<i>But if it goes from A to B or vice-versa, 
the chest core lights up for a second.</i>

16:55.880 --> 16:58.080
<i>This allows for some limited 
anticipation of its attacks.</i>

16:58.080 --> 16:59.420
<i>Given the difference between my 
height and the golem's height,</i>

16:59.420 --> 17:02.820
<i>that generates some predictability 
in attacks from sides A and B.</i>

17:02.820 --> 17:04.370
<i>I had a theory that the 
moment I dodged an attack</i>

17:04.370 --> 17:06.040
<i>or the action's attack hit box faded,</i>

17:06.040 --> 17:09.530
<i>I could jump on the arm to jump 
up and directly attack the core.</i>

17:09.530 --> 17:12.230
<i>But when I actually tried it, I ended 
up repelled by an invisible energy field</i>

17:12.230 --> 17:14.940
<i>which shaved 70% off my HP,</i>

17:14.940 --> 17:15.850
<i>so I was forced to change my strategy,</i>

17:15.850 --> 17:17.620
<i>which turned out to be directly peeling 
off its armor to expose a weak point—</i>

17:17.410 --> 17:22.220
Practical Training  Opponent 9
Beta Unit Golem S2

17:17.620 --> 17:19.100
Oh, screw it!

17:19.100 --> 17:21.240
I dodged, stripped it down, hit it, and won!

17:21.080 --> 17:22.220
<b>Defeated on
7th try</b>

17:25.230 --> 17:28.540
Hell yeah! Just one left!

17:31.540 --> 17:35.990
Practical Training  Opponent 9
Beta Unit Golem S2

17:31.680 --> 17:35.240
<i>Practical training, opponent 9: 
Beta Unit Golem S2, complete.</i>

17:34.740 --> 17:35.990
<b>Complete</b>

17:37.450 --> 17:39.800
<i>Although...</i>

17:39.800 --> 17:44.310
<i>All that fighting to go up two measly levels?</i>

17:44.310 --> 17:49.930
<i>Thanks so much, Vorpal Soul Collar which 
so generously cuts my exp gains in half...</i>

17:51.730 --> 17:54.840
Sunraku-san! You should 
probably take a break!

17:54.280 --> 17:57.510
<b>Menacing</b>

17:54.840 --> 17:57.510
You have a great and 
terrible look in your eyes!

17:57.510 --> 17:59.630
Whatcha mean?

17:59.630 --> 18:03.390
All this optimization is going great for me!

18:03.780 --> 18:07.270
Now, bring out the last monster already!

18:07.970 --> 18:09.850
Well, well.

18:11.860 --> 18:14.970
You beat the ninth already, did you?

18:15.840 --> 18:17.400
Guess it's perfect timing.

18:17.880 --> 18:19.160
Vash?

18:19.160 --> 18:21.570
Dadd—I mean, Boss!

18:24.600 --> 18:26.400
<i>"Perfect timing," huh?</i>

18:26.400 --> 18:30.040
<i>Beating the ninth monster triggered 
the event flag, I'll bet.</i>

18:30.380 --> 18:32.360
So, Aniki.

18:32.670 --> 18:35.050
Would that last monster happen to be...

18:35.320 --> 18:40.630
I thought I'd make your tenth 
opponent a monster I caught.

18:40.960 --> 18:42.550
I went on a bit of an excursion for it.

19:00.410 --> 19:03.690
A human? Yeah, don't think so...

19:04.480 --> 19:06.040
A sorcerer type?

19:06.410 --> 19:09.350
